    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27862" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mangōnico</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-izo</span></b> ), āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a.
		mango, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to set off, deck, adorn</i> an article for sale (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ita pueros mangonicavit saepe obstetrix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					32, 10, 47, § 135</span></i>
			. —In <i>part. perf.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mangonicatae villae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 54, 79, § 168</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			gen., <i>to set off, adorn</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					23, 1, 16, § 26</span></i>
			.</div>
